#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:138
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:141
msgid ""
"Options can either be specified as query parameters of the `<script "
"src=\"..../livereload.js\">` tag's source URL, or as a global "
"`window.LiveReloadOptions` dictionary. If the dictionary is specified, "
"`livereload.js` does not even try looking for its `<script>` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:143
msgid "The set of supported options is the same for both methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:145
msgid ""
"`host`: the host that runs a LiveReload server; required if specifying "
"`LiveReloadOptions`, otherwise will be autodetected as the origin of the "
"`<script>` tag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:146
msgid "`port`: optional server port override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:147
msgid "`path`: optional path to livereload server (default: 'livereload')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:148
msgid ""
"`mindelay`, `maxdelay`: range of reconnection delays (if `livereload.js` "
"cannot connect to the server, it will attempt to reconnect with "
"increasing delays); defaults to 1,000 ms minimum and 60,000 ms maximum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:149
msgid ""
"`handshake_timeout`: timeout for a protocol handshake to be completed "
"after a connection attempt; mostly only needed if you're running an "
"interactive debugger on your web socket server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:150
msgid ""
"`isChromeExtension`: reload chrome runtime instead of page when true "
"(default: false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:151
msgid ""
"`reloadMissingCSS`: prevent reload of CSS when changed stylesheet isn't "
"found in page (default: true)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:154
msgid "Issues & Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:157
msgid ""
"**Live reloading of imported stylesheets has a 200ms lag.** Modifying a "
"CSS `@import` rule to reference a not-yet-cached file causes WebKit to "
"lose all document styles, so we have to apply a workaround that causes a "
"lag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:159
msgid ""
"Our workaround is to add a temporary `<link />` element for the imported "
"stylesheet we're trying to reload, wait 200ms to make sure WebKit loads "
"the new file, then remove `<link />` and recreate the `@import` rule. "
"This prevents a flash of unstyled content. (We also wait 200 more "
"milliseconds and recreate the `@import` rule again, in case those initial"
" 200ms were not enough.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:161
msgid ""
"**Live image reloading is limited to `<img src=\"...\" />`, `background-"
"image` and `border-image` styles.** Any other places where images can be "
"mentioned?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/livereload-js_README.md:163
msgid ""
"**Live image reloading is limited to `jpg`, `jpeg`, `gif`, and `png` "
"extensions.** Maybe need to add `svg` there? Anything else?"
msgstr ""

